  "clipAttribution": {
   "title": "Radial Nerve Block at the Elbow",
   "caption": "50s M with PMH IVDU presented with a dorsal hand abscess. To facilitate I&D, a radial nerve block was performed at the level of the elbow using the linear transducer and an in-plane approach. Injection of anesthetic seen adjacent to the radial nerve (*). The hyperechoic distal humeral cortex can be seen at the right of the image. Shortly after the block, I&D was able to be performed at bedside.\nDr. Michael Heffler, PGY3\nDenver Health Residency in Emergency Medicine",
